---
description: UI component and styling conventions
globs: "**/*.{ts,tsx,css,module.css}"
alwaysApply: true
---

- Before creating UI, search for an existing component. Reuse it when it fits, extend it when extension is sufficient, and compose existing primitives before creating a new component. Create one only when none fit; do not duplicate existing behavior or styling with minor differences.
- Keep reusable UI semantic, accessible, business-logic-free, and mobile-first.

Theme specifications and shared appearance, color, elevation, and layer policies live under `ui/common/src/design-system/theme/`.
Before changing reusable UI, read `ui/web/src/design-system/Overview.mdx` and the relevant linked design-system page.
Before implementing or changing palettes, shades, appearance, or interaction states, read and follow `ui/web/src/design-system/colors/Colors.mdx` and `ui/web/src/design-system/Theming.mdx`.

Shared reusable components require a common API/value logic in `@ui/common` and thin renderers in both `@web-ui` and `@mobile-ui`.

### Component Structure

Compose components from focused subcomponents recursively. Extract a section when it has its own visual purpose, interactions, styling, state, or meaningful name. Parent components orchestrate data and composition; leaf components own rendering details.

Each component must live in a file named after it. A tiny helper component may remain with its only parent when it has no independent meaning or reuse. Module-scope constants and helpers used by only one component remain in that component's file.

Every new or changed UI component needs a matching platform story. Public reusable components need `Playground with Live code editor` and `Gallery` stories. Use inferred `argTypes`; specify only non-inferable controls or mappings.

Reserve final layout dimensions before optional or asynchronous content appears; toggling content must not move surrounding UI.

Buttons use square corners by default. Circle and hexagon buttons are icon-only and require an accessible label.

### Web
- Apps and gears must use components from `@web-ui` when an appropriate component exists.
- Inside `@web-ui`, use native semantic elements (`<hr>`, `<button>`, `<nav>`, `<label>`, etc.) instead of generic `<div>` elements.
- Interactive elements must support keyboard use and include ARIA attributes when needed.
- Use CSS modules.
- Class names use kebab-case.
- Use `className` instead of inline `style`.
- Use inline `style` only for runtime-computed values that cannot use classes or CSS variables.
- Use CSS variables for theming.
- Never use `!important`.

### Mobile
- Use `StyleSheet.create` for styles.
- Define `StyleSheet.create` before props and components.
- Do not use CSS modules or CSS custom properties.
